{"description":"Show which devices are online, each device's custom status, and when an offline device was last seen.\n\nThe non-negotiable part: presence is derived by the coordinator from an observed heartbeat with a liveness TTL. Client-announced presence is rejected outright, because a device that is killed or loses power cannot send a goodbye and would otherwise stay 'online' forever — which in an emergency-communication tool is worse than showing nothing.","acceptanceCriteria":"1. A connecting device appears online to every other connected device.\n2. A device disconnecting cleanly appears offline with a last-seen timestamp.\n3. A device whose process is killed with SIGKILL appears offline within the liveness TTL, having announced nothing. This is the defining test for this item.\n4. A custom status survives the setting device's reconnect.\n5. No code path lets a client assert its own online state.\n6. Works on a build without the `voice` tag."}